{
  "schema_version": "metric-identity-registry.v1",
  "description": "Canonical Atlas metric identity authority. metric_id is the canonical identifier used by execution contracts (primary_metric/secondary_metrics). Every layer resolves metric names through this registry: native training (aliases.training), scientific reproduction (aliases.scientific), and the public API projection (aliases.public is the published key; aliases.public_input lists additional raw names the public projection accepts). direction states whether a higher or lower value is better; sklearn_scorer is the scikit-learn scorer string used when a metric drives estimator scoring (null when no built-in scorer exists); positive_class_sensitive marks binary metrics whose value depends on which class is positive, so a scorer must be bound to the governed positive class. Adding a metric is a change to this file only; historical artifacts keep the names they were written with.",
